*.tar.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Route-map bundles under worlds/<seed>/. These patterns are deliberately glob-based rather
# than per-seed, so adding a world costs nothing here -- worldgen changes every pack version,
# so there will be one bundle per seed per version.
#
# Rasters are binary and regenerable. loot.json is ~1.6 MB of minified single-line JSON: it
# would be stored as text, but a one-line file does not produce a useful diff, so every
# rebuild would append a fresh 1.6 MB blob to history for no reviewable benefit.
worlds/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
worlds/**/loot.json filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# meta.json, palette.json, pois.json and veins.json stay as text on purpose: they are small,
# and being able to read a bundle's provenance and counts in a diff is worth more than the
# bytes. The builder writes them one record per line so that diff is actually legible.
